.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>TickerTrends’ latest private-market tracking puts <strong>Anthropic at roughly $74.1 billion in annualized revenue run rate</strong>, versus <strong>$41.3 billion for OpenAI</strong>.</p><p>Anthropic is currently tracking at about 1.79 times OpenAI’s ARR, a gap of roughly $32.8 billion. Since the companies’ last reported figures, Anthropic has increased 57.7%, while OpenAI has increased 65.2%.</p><p>Anthropic’s tracked ARR rose from $10.2 billion in January to $35.6 billion in April, $69.6 billion in June, and $74.1 billion in July.</p><p>OpenAI’s tracked ARR increased from $21.4 billion in January to $33.0 billion in May and $41.3 billion in July.</p><p>Anthropic remains materially ahead in absolute ARR, while <strong>OpenAI has posted the stronger increase since its latest reported figure</strong>.</p>",
